### Edge cases also tested (`nil_edge_cases.go`)

| Edge case | Behaviour | Verdict |
|-----------|-----------|---------|
| **Nil slice** `var s []int` | `len(s)=0`, range loops zero times | ✅ Safe |
| **Nil map read** `m["key"]` | Returns zero value, no panic | ✅ Safe |
| **Nil map write** `m["key"] = 1` | **Panics** — must initialize (`make`) | ⚠️ Dangerous |
| **Interface with nil concrete** `(*MyError)(nil)` in `error` variable | `err != nil` despite concrete value being nil — classic Go trap | ⚠️ Trap |
| **Nil pointer receiver method** | Works if method checks `if s == nil` | ✅ Defensible |
| **Nil interface** `var iface interface{} = nil` | `iface == nil` is true | ✅ Correct |

